# Trivy vulnerability exceptions — one CVE ID per line, with a comment
# explaining why it's safe to ignore. Prefer fixing over adding entries
# here; only add when there's a genuine, documented reason a real finding
# doesn't apply.

# --- apps/api image: Debian packages pulled in by `playwright install
# --with-deps chromium` (see apps/api/Dockerfile). All of these are marked
# "affected" by Trivy with no fixed version yet published for Debian
# bookworm — `apt-get upgrade` (already run in the Dockerfile) has nothing
# newer to install. None of this is reachable application attack surface:
# it's OS packages installed for Chromium's benefit, never invoked over the
# network, and specifically xserver-common/xvfb are dead weight since the
# FFF scraper (apps/api/src/fff-sync/fff-scraper.service.ts) always runs
# Chromium in headless mode and never starts an X server at all.
